From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 17:26:04 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 263/333] [ae-patch] Stop the dock's Compact card clipping its
 buttons on a phone

On a narrow screen the card's "336k tokens" label kept its full width while the
strip clipped what did not fit, so Compact was cut off and Not now was gone. The
label now truncates first, and the strip drops Not now on a phone (the opened
tray keeps it), so Compact always shows whole.
---
 web/src/components/AeActionDock.test.tsx | 2 ++
 web/src/components/AeActionDock.tsx      | 9 +++++----
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/web/src/components/AeActionDock.test.tsx b/web/src/components/AeActionDock.test.tsx
index 7136eca4e0e57b369635191673bcdfe5d59b0d7f..4431881ae45f1d7452e44df1b746397c39e170e0 100644
--- a/web/src/components/AeActionDock.test.tsx
+++ b/web/src/components/AeActionDock.test.tsx
@@ -1042,6 +1042,8 @@ describe("the Compact card", () => {
     );
     expect(within(lead).getByTestId("ae-dock-compact")).toBeTruthy();
     expect(within(lead).getByTestId("ae-dock-context-later")).toBeTruthy();
+    // On a phone the strip drops Not now so Compact is never clipped; the tray keeps it.
+    expect(within(lead).getByTestId("ae-dock-context-later").className).toContain("hidden");
   });
 
   it("is absent without the label, when snoozed, or for a different open chat", async () => {
